                    <nc xml:id="m-71d2c6b5-5c11-4b8c-a840-cd981af73c42" pname="c" oct="4" />
                  </neume>
                </syllable>
                <custos xml:id="m-a55bfa9f-517c-4ec9-bb8c-14e2d8436043" facs="#m-dc835828-e521-4826-b6e7-9117161364ad" pname="c" oct="4" />
              </layer>
            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-8844b45c-6c12-4cec-8058-722f587d1699">
              <lg xml:id="m-c94c7dba-d6ce-41d7-bb74-360f91a3f4c1">
                <l xml:id="m-c58880b9-b190-4642-bc5c-47cd61b8555b" facs="#m-b3ece2d1-9ed1-4c1a-b1d7-2c70f9327576" label="text-like">The Common Tones of the Mass.</l><l xml:id="m-05be5f3c-6e83-4c35-9ce1-79de3f82b1be" facs="#m-2971d9b1-c607-4440-baaf-83ca32b37049" label="ambiguous">101</l><l xml:id="m-c57fe611-381d-416a-a568-72b22407289f" facs="#m-3516e8ed-f11f-4a94-bffd-dc1c0ba93c3d" label="text-like">Examples of the full stop</l><l xml:id="m-7caef78d-f619-4a21-9e43-f9f8890233e1" facs="#m-d786c3c8-a351-41c7-aec5-3f2225c014cf" label="lyrics-like">ve-tústa sér- vi¬ tus té¬</l><l xml:id="m-cd90a022-fdb9-42f4-b691-c6126d9349e6" facs="#m-8aa982ad-9e3e-49c3-8e94-664c1f564f17" label="ambiguous">net.</l><l xml:id="m-bae65900-69a9-486d-aaf7-423daa2e4e7b" facs="#m-6d9b6860-ac37-4d95-b2c5-c1fca778052b" label="lyrics-like">pérfru¬</l><l xml:id="m-ddd2cf60-5aea-4f2f-816b-6e999be8d1bd" facs="#m-bd83ab6c-3fc1-4a8f-a38b-086cff613973" label="ambiguous">lae- ti- ti- a.</l><l xml:id="m-6ecb457d-6c0b-40a1-b898-5c18638a909b" facs="#m-07d79805-bdd3-4ed9-a5c3-bd28c93c0af6" label="lyrics-like">di- gná-tus es. (A).</l><l xml:id="m-5bd85cbb-a8a6-4f2a-a4fa-4e733e796e70" facs="#m-51210e17-6edc-4549-abf7-26d61feaf4b5" label="lyrics-like">or: di- gná- tus es. (B).</l><l xml:id="m-3d62999d-e546-4f0a-a012-54345cf7f673" facs="#m-997157bd-eeef-4a9d-b953-3eb44ab59424" label="text-like">Prayer of St. Stephen.</l><l xml:id="m-f6fd01a3-4354-4c4a-826e-37884c531203" facs="#m-bd5fe9cc-a40a-447b-9fc2-a99cd5366700" label="lyrics-like">Full stoṕ. Conclusion.</l><l xml:id="m-9c3f6d69-4150-48f7-a3c4-535b8269fbbe" facs="#m-5decc18a-6419-4e5a-a3d2-c5315d84eb2e" label="lyrics-like">Jésum Chrístum Fi-li-um tú-um. Qui técum ví-vit et régnat...</l><l xml:id="m-f09ec030-c26f-4275-b837-17e4484c0e12" facs="#m-b3302570-6a54-43b3-b6b9-022c34e1220b" label="text-like">In this tone, the Prayer has only the fex, which occurs at the end of the</l><l xml:id="m-e0a09d9f-ff84-45bb-94b6-0a20f1340d63" facs="#m-771217f8-4efd-49ce-9a56-7f371435739a" label="ambiguous">first sub-division.</l><l xml:id="m-eff11a9d-db70-4e42-8259-649f7944ca06" facs="#m-80c9f804-184e-4863-92dd-b39be3fb62f5" label="text-like">After the flex, as after any pause, the first syllable of the following word</l><l xml:id="m-0b64ce3f-f494-4a9f-ac11-b17d09d2a07c" facs="#m-14916431-aca1-4515-b91e-af534d92ed2d" label="text-like">starts a tone lower than the dominant.</l><l xml:id="m-ef5ea89d-f85f-4736-bcfb-5bfa968e66f7" facs="#m-7f8faf53-7654-4e40-bb39-5ff79bfed300" label="lyrics-like">If the Prarer is longer than usual tas, for instance, the Prayers A cúnctis.</l><l xml:id="m-5617af0b-c854-4d36-8d98-e62ca4cda6ae" facs="#m-0c840d1e-742a-4562-8184-8aca6776e3b5" label="lyrics-like">and Omnipotens sempitérne Déus) the formúla of the full ston may be repeatea</l><l xml:id="m-af1ed651-fff4-482a-a87c-f116190f0026" facs="#m-85c5b2d6-7b43-4f3c-98c2-c94b821087c1" label="text-like">on condition that it be preceded each time by a flex.</l><l xml:id="m-2350f9b0-43ba-4602-a63e-3777eabfff98" facs="#m-363ceeb6-7365-4333-9ffb-0b41ef84f371" label="lyrics-like">When the Prayer is preceded by Flectámus génua:</l><l xml:id="m-063bf5e4-d385-45d8-84c9-2baae9c96d65" facs="#m-c7dca03b-0904-412c-9e6c-26ad51dedbb0" label="lyrics-like">Orémus. Flectámus génu-a. Levá-te. Pópu-lum tú-um...</l><l xml:id="m-8d2cb0fb-206b-4f38-8139-5baf4fa66123" facs="#m-73bfa104-bbc2-4b89-9fd0-f86093fcbd8c" label="lyrics-like">(When the Y. Dóminus vobiscum. has to be replaced by the V. Dómine</l><l xml:id="m-f790b9d2-76c8-4c0b-8e17-9509b1f78e4e" facs="#m-91abc8fa-3cb3-48aa-8175-f6546e90e657" label="lyrics-like">exáudi. the folloming is used:</l><l xml:id="m-aecd178e-256f-409a-a1ca-ed0d82b9eb17" facs="#m-c50ae44b-e420-461a-9efb-35adedc2c1c1" label="lyrics-like">V. Dómine exáudi ora-ti-ónem mé-am. R. Et clámor mé-us ad te</l><l xml:id="m-b36f585f-b26a-468c-a3fc-631643f3fb66" facs="#m-59830b84-6987-4676-a2e4-428e03eb4a87" label="lyrics-like">véni-at.)</l><l xml:id="m-7ce9c55f-2661-443f-b4e4-5aa1d086d95b" facs="#m-5fb31a48-928d-4c93-882a-84b02df9b468" label="ambiguous">b) Simple Tone.</l><l xml:id="m-4aad8b7e-fc8b-4032-a850-04433630789d" facs="#m-92f85068-a3f9-42a0-83d4-ab51ebfff5d4" label="text-like">This tone is used for the Prayers of the Aspersion, ot the Blessings,</l><l xml:id="m-8845f8db-3c2d-468f-9382-1406ffe8f4c5" facs="#m-babc6852-15ca-49ad-a974-4aa601f61755" label="text-like">of the Litanies, and for other Prayers of the same kind, except those which</l><l xml:id="m-ae7f0ed6-7bf4-4349-828a-b8a875b3d2e0" facs="#m-9f41b198-553b-4554-a7e4-dd945637d19b" label="lyrics-like">are preceded by Flectámus génua.</l><l xml:id="m-600ba836-26ab-4e65-9ead-d9be2159628e" facs="#m-4dd9f4ea-defc-4a0d-97a7-11253de2bd4d" label="lyrics-like">If this simple tone be adopted, it is used also for the Prayer Super pópulum.</l><l xml:id="m-b56743bf-e910-4c89-b5f2-1987cf9bf5ed" facs="#m-ecf3c1e4-8d8f-4f6e-b416-057b005bf3d0" label="lyrics-like">after the admonition Humiliãte cápita véstra. (as on p. 90).</l><l xml:id="m-2e4c3ccf-d58b-43ea-bd52-15cb8268a316" facs="#m-5cdcf1f3-58ad-47ca-84c2-db274764e8e7" label="lyrics-like">DOminus vobíscum. R. Et cum spí-ri-tu tú-o. Orémus.</l><l xml:id="m-b7118ab6-b068-4e7e-aee8-c1155092850b" facs="#m-d00aff8a-aadf-446f-af57-f084c62eb345" label="ambiguous">Flex.</l><l xml:id="m-d648ac59-1a7b-47c6-8218-4c3d092f42da" facs="#m-6bad5846-411f-40c2-9f02-2503cbb2349e" label="lyrics-like">Praésta, quaésumus omnípotens Dé-us: t ut semper ra-ti-onabí-li-a</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>